public class ContactTriggerHandler {

    public static void execute() {
        if (Trigger.isBefore) {
            handleBefore();
        }
        if (Trigger.isAfter && Trigger.isInsert) {
            handleAfterInsert();
        }
    }

    private static void handleBefore() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null) {
                accountIds.add(c.AccountId);
            }
        }

        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, Account> accountMap = new Map<Id, Account>(
            [SELECT BillingCountry, AccountSource FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds]
        );

        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null) {
                Account a = accountMap.get(c.AccountId);
                if (a != null) {
                    if (String.isBlank(c.MailingCountry)) {
                        c.MailingCountry = a.BillingCountry;
                    }
                    if (Trigger.isInsert && String.isBlank(c.LeadSource)) {
                        c.LeadSource = a.AccountSource;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    private static void handleAfterInsert() {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null && String.isNotBlank(c.Phone)) {
                accountIds.add(c.AccountId);
            }
        }

        if (accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, Account> accountMap = new Map<Id, Account>(
            [SELECT Id, Phone FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds]
        );

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();

        for (Contact c : Trigger.new) {
            if (c.AccountId != null && String.isNotBlank(c.Phone)) {
                Account a = accountMap.get(c.AccountId);
                if (a != null && String.isBlank(a.Phone)) {
                    a.Phone = c.Phone;
                    accountsToUpdate.add(a);
                }
            }
        }

        if (!accountsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update accountsToUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

**How the budget is met:**

| Context | SOQL | DML |
|---|---|---|
| Before (insert or update) | 1 – `SELECT … WHERE Id IN :accountIds` | 0 |
| After insert | 1 – `SELECT Id, Phone WHERE Id IN :accountIds` | 1 – `update accountsToUpdate` |
| **Total** | **2** | **1** |

**How the "first contact wins" detail is preserved:**

The `accountMap` holds a single `Account` object reference per Id. When the first eligible contact sets `a.Phone = c.Phone`, that same object is what every subsequent lookup returns. By the time the second contact for the same account is processed, `a.Phone` is no longer blank, so the `String.isBlank(a.Phone)` guard skips it — exactly matching the original row-by-row behaviour where each iteration re-queried and saw the already-updated phone.

