```java
public class PicklistService {

    public class Option {
        public String value { get; set; }
        public String label { get; set; }
        public Boolean isDefault { get; set; }
    }

    public class PicklistServiceException extends Exception {}

    public static List<Option> activeOptions(String objectApiName, String fieldApiName) {
        // Validate inputs
        if (String.isBlank(objectApiName) || String.isBlank(fieldApiName)) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object and field API names must not be null or blank.');
        }

        // Resolve object (case-insensitive)
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult sObjectDesc;
        try {
            sObjectDesc = Schema.describeSObject(objectApiName);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object does not exist: ' + objectApiName);
        }

        if (sObjectDesc == null) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object does not exist: ' + objectApiName);
        }

        // Resolve field case-insensitively from the field map
        Map<String, Schema.SObjectField> fieldMap = sObjectDesc.getFieldMap();
        Schema.SObjectField sObjectField = null;
        for (String key : fieldMap.keySet()) {
            if (key.equalsIgnoreCase(fieldApiName)) {
                sObjectField = fieldMap.get(key);
                break;
            }
        }

        if (sObjectField == null) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field does not exist on object ' + sObjectDesc.getName() + ': ' + fieldApiName);
        }

        // Verify the field is a picklist or multi-select picklist
        Schema.DescribeFieldResult fieldDesc = sObjectField.getDescribe();
        if (fieldDesc.getType() != Schema.DisplayType.PICKLIST
            && fieldDesc.getType() != Schema.DisplayType.MULTIPICKLIST) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field is not a picklist or multi-select picklist: ' + fieldDesc.getName());
        }

        // Build the result – active values only, in defined order
        List<Schema.PicklistEntry> entries = fieldDesc.getPicklistValues();
        List<Option> result = new List<Option>();

        for (Schema.PicklistEntry entry : entries) {
            if (entry.isValid()) {
                Option opt = new Option();
                opt.value     = entry.getValue();
                opt.label     = entry.getLabel();
                opt.isDefault = entry.getDefault();
                result.add(opt);
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

**How it works, point by point:**

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Null / blank guard | `String.isBlank` on both parameters → `PicklistServiceException` |
| Object not found | `Schema.describeSObject` is case-insensitive; returns `null` (or throws) for unknown objects → caught and re-thrown as `PicklistServiceException` |
| Field not found | Iterates `getFieldMap().keySet()` with `equalsIgnoreCase` so `INDUSTRY` matches `Industry`; if no match → `PicklistServiceException` |
| Wrong field type | Checks `DescribeFieldResult.getType()` against `PICKLIST` and `MULTIPICKLIST` |
| Active values only | `PicklistEntry.isValid()` is `false` for inactive values; they are skipped |
| Defined order | `getPicklistValues()` returns entries in the order they are defined on the field |
| `isDefault` | `PicklistEntry.getDefault()` returns `true` only for the field's default value |
| No leaking exceptions | All failure paths throw `PicklistServiceException`; the `try/catch` around `describeSObject` prevents any unexpected runtime exception from escaping |

