```apex
public class AccountScoringJob implements Queueable {

    private List<Id> accountIds;

    public AccountScoringJob(List<Id> accountIds) {
        this.accountIds = accountIds;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Integer batchSize = Math.min(200, accountIds.size());
        List<Id> batchIds = accountIds.subList(0, batchSize);

        List<Account> accounts = [SELECT Id, AnnualRevenue FROM Account WHERE Id IN :batchIds];

        for (Account acc : accounts) {
            if (acc.AnnualRevenue != null && acc.AnnualRevenue >= 1000000) {
                acc.Rating = 'Hot';
            } else if (acc.AnnualRevenue != null && acc.AnnualRevenue >= 100000) {
                acc.Rating = 'Warm';
            } else {
                acc.Rating = 'Cold';
            }
        }

        if (!accounts.isEmpty()) {
            update accounts;
        }

        if (batchSize < accountIds.size()) {
            List<Id> remaining = accountIds.subList(batchSize, accountIds.size());
            System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(remaining));
        }
    }

    public static Id start(List<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }
        return System.enqueueJob(new AccountScoringJob(accountIds));
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| ≤ 200 per execution | `Math.min(200, accountIds.size())` slices the first 200 |
| 1 SOQL + 1 DML per execution | Single `SELECT … WHERE Id IN :batchIds` then a single `update accounts` |
| Chain | After processing, if `batchSize < accountIds.size()`, a new `AccountScoringJob` is enqueued with the remainder |
| `start()` guard | Returns `null` for null/empty list without enqueueing |
| `execute(null)` safe | The `QueueableContext` parameter is never dereferenced |
| Works in a single test for 50 000 Ids | 250 chained jobs; `Test.stopTest()` executes all enqueued Queueable jobs (including those enqueued by prior jobs) synchronously, and each job gets its own governor-limit context (1 SOQL + 1 DML per job is well within limits) |

